/* The redaction plate's alpha, registered so it can be transitioned: an
   unregistered custom property flips at the end of its transition instead
   of passing through values, and the plate's background reads it through
   color-mix(). 1 is the covered plate, 0 the cleared one [scope-94]. */
@property --kp-redact-alpha {
    syntax: '<number>';
    inherits: false;
    initial-value: 0;
}

/* The bar's mega menu is held on screen while a transition on the panel plays (js/components.js
   settleClosing()): this number, which pastel transitions over the sheet's time, is that transition
   (review round 2, 2026-10-13; brutalism's --kp-sig-br-hold). */
@property --kp-sig-pastel-hold {
    syntax: '<number>';
    inherits: false;
    initial-value: 0;
}

@layer kp.register {

/* ── Signature: pastel's grammar [scope-141] ───────────────────────────── */
/* Kenny approved pastel's character in full on 2026-10-14 03:23
   (research/pastel-character/decided.json, themes/pastel/CHARACTER.md §1,
   G1-G20): a risograph-printed sticker sheet in a planner. Everything that
   happens here happens to paper: it is PRINTED TWICE AND STUCK ON. A part's
   second pass (a flat silhouette in the second ink, --fx-overprint, no words)
   springs from a wide misregistration into its rest 6 px off register, down
   and toward the end, where it stays as the part's flat shadow; 120 ms later
   the part itself swings down from its top-start corner onto it, on the soft
   landing (one 8 % overshoot, settled once). One landing is 560 ms; a close
   is that landing played backwards, frame for frame. A part fixed to the
   page then has a thumbtack pushed in at its top centre, which comes out
   first when it leaves. Hover peels the top-end corner into a fold, focus is
   the dashed line alone, a press sticks the part down flat, a live change
   wobbles, and loading is the pom-pom caterpillar: everything that waits
   becomes caterpillar (js/loading-pieces.js adds its pom-poms, head and
   legs; the spinner is the caterpillar going round a day sticker).

   HOW THE TWO PASSES ARE TWO LAYERS. The demo draws the pass and the part as
   two sibling boxes, so the part can be invisible while its pass is already
   there. In the package a part is one element, and its opacity and its turn
   carry everything inside it, pseudo-elements included; so the pass is
   drawn OUTSIDE the part wherever the part can be faded as a whole:
     A. a part in the top layer (a dialog, a popover, a menu, the date
        picker's panel, the combobox's list): its own ::backdrop, placed on
        the part by anchor positioning (`position-anchor: auto`, which reads
        the part's layout box, never its turn). A modal's dim is that
        backdrop's 200vmax border, so a click outside still reaches it;
     A2. a part hanging in its holder (the bar's dropdown and mega menu, a
        tooltip): the holder's ::after, anchored to the part
        (`anchor-scope` keeps the name to the holder);
   and where neither exists (a toast, an alert, the tour's card, the side
   navigation, the busy panels), the part draws its own plate and pass:
     B. the plate is its ::after and the pass its ::before, both under its
        words; the part does not fade as a whole, its plate and its children
        follow `--kp-sig-pa-ink`, and the pass counter-turns against the
        part's swing, so on screen it only slides, as the demo's does.
   Two registered numbers carry the clock (--kp-sig-pa-pass for the pass,
   --kp-sig-pa-ink for the part), so anything that reads them follows the
   one animation that runs; js/motion.js keeps and reverses that animation
   (and a ::backdrop's) for every close, so a close stays the open backwards.

   Without anchor positioning (`@supports not (anchor-name: --a)`) every
   part shows its pass at rest as a flat box-shadow and opens with the swing
   alone. Every motion sits under prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference; the
   reduced pose is the finished picture (G19). Colours are tokens only. */

@property --kp-sig-pa-ink {
    syntax: '<number>';
    inherits: true;
    initial-value: 1;
}

@property --kp-sig-pa-pass {
    syntax: '<number>';
    inherits: true;
    initial-value: 1;
}

